  bootwright / catalog media purge
      Purge entries from this controller's catalog. By default, entries named in any saved
      context's input or reserved by an operation are kept. --force also deletes referenced and
      reserved entries, which can prevent later apply, retry or destroy until the same data is
      restored. It does not bypass active operations or store integrity checks. --dry-run only
      shows what would be deleted. Otherwise confirm the plan or use --yes.

  Usage
    bootwright catalog media purge [flags]

  Command flags
      --dry-run  Show the purge plan without deleting anything
      --force    Include referenced and reserved entries
      --yes      Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright catalog media purge --dry-run
